#Application Architecture.

Important: I do not want to include a Domain Layer. Please don't include a domain layer and Use Cases unies instructed otherwise.
Important: I want the top level packaging to be featured based. So the First package will be articles. Inside the articles package I want only 3 packages: ui, presentation and data.

* UI Layer
- Single Activity app with Composables
- Navigation components

* Presentation Layer
- ViewModels
- UI State classes
- Presentation models, eg. Article.

* Data layer
- Repository implementations
- Remote Data Sources (API)
- Data Models, eg. ArticleData
- NO database or local storage needed
- Repository Pattern. No interface only repository implementation. Single source of truth. Easy to switch data sources.

* MVVM Pattern
- ViewModels handle UI logic and UIState 
- Composables are responsible only for UI
- State classes represent UI state

* Dependency injection
- We'll use Hilt dependency injection

* Coroutines & State Flow
- Coroutines for asynchronous operations
- Handle API calls and data processing
- State Flow between View Model and UI for Manage UI State update

* Key concepts
- Clean Architecture
- Important: Simplicity
- Separation of concerns
- Testability
- Maintainability
- I don't want you to create any base classes

I want to follow a packaging structure as in the following example:

com.erick.herrera.daylyai
├── DaylyAIApplication.kt
├── MainActivity.kt
├── ui
│   └── theme
│       ├── Color.kt
│       ├── Theme.kt
│       └── Type.kt
└── articles
    ├── data
    │   ├── ArticleApi.kt
    │   ├── ArticleData.kt
    │   ├── ArticleRepository.kt
    │   ├── ArticlesResponse.kt
    │   └── NetworkModule.kt
    ├── presentation
    │   ├── Article.kt
    │   ├── ArticleUIState.kt
    │   └── ArticleViewModel.kt
    └── ui
        ├── ArticleScreen.kt
        └── ArticleUIStateProvider.kt
